{"title":"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, each small square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm. The area of the shaded region, in square centimeters is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af7dba70b246621c30f416c12b618043f78e2d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2.75 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3.25 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4.5 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"449\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of the shaded region, we can subtract the unshaded region from the total area.\n</p><p>We can first label the lengths of the legs of the triangles. The unshaded region consists of two right triangles, as all of the angles of a square are right angles.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The total area is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> with a side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm, meaning that we can find that the area is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb56d5e7cbea7b901a5c559c43b1cb77b4b0716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2 = 9$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> square cm\n</p><p>We then can find the area of each of the triangles using the formula for the area of a triangle, and add them together:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/93232f76992d7816b74dc27eefe5ef10ff168c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\times 3}{2} = \\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/704a2896f56b5a8e05a3885b1b132160388eaec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\times 1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Adding these, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbf84a23c4e329e5e7568c1609d3927289906484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{2} + \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{9 + 3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/3771419483e60aa0384264e301e91aec7a03d66d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{12}{2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" /> square cm\n</p><p>Subtracting this from the total area, we get that the unshaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d928e832c7ee51a1fd06248d8fe9ef77cfabc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - 6 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"122\" height=\"30\" /> square cm.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the height of the shaded triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm, and its base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can now use the formula for the area of a triangle to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25f7cf73d038c92825118fe49110d0a0bfbde2c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\times 2}{2} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" /> square cm\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal\">1999 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" t